From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 15:20:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 005/220] [ae-patch] Add a split view that shows up to four
 sessions side by side

omnigent-ae patch P5 (2026-09-24). "Open in split view" on a sidebar
session's menu (kebab or right-click, any row, desktop only) opens
/split?s=a,b with the session being viewed and the chosen one. Up to four
panes, each a full session with its composer, a session switcher, an
"open alone" button and a close button. Dividers drag or take the arrow
keys; the layout is kept in local storage and a bare /split restores it.
Below 1024px the route shows the first pane's session on its own.

Each pane is a frame of the ordinary /c/:id route. The chat store is a
module-scope singleton with one foreground conversation, so ChatPage
cannot render twice in one React tree; a frame gives each pane its own
store, streams and keyboard focus without touching the store. The page
polls each frame's location once a second so a pane that opens another
session inside itself keeps the layout in step.

Logic lives in three new files (lib/aeSplitLayout.ts, pages/AeSplitPage.tsx,
shell/AeSplitMenuItem.tsx). The upstream edits are ten lines: the /split
route outside AppShell in App.tsx, the item after P4's Status submenu in
Sidebar.tsx, and one condition in AppShell's initialSidebarOpen so a pane
starts with its sidebar closed. Tests: aeSplitLayout.test.ts,
AeSplitPage.test.tsx and three cases in Sidebar.aeStatus.test.tsx.

